aph"><i>Initial solution.</i> The GA mentioned in section 2.1 and SA are th=
e same with generating the initial solution, which is based on the preproce=
ssed (time period, classroom) mapping and satisfies the unavailability cons=
traint. In addition, both use the same fitness function to measure the numb=
er of hard constraint conflicts, thus ensuring the consistency of the evalu=
ation criteria.</div><div role=3D"paragraph"><i>Neighbourhood generation.</=
i> In each cooling iteration, we generate a neighbouring solution by select=
ing one random course and reassigning it to a different (timeslot, room) pa=
ir from its valid assignment map, and also use the same fitness function to=
 validate the neighbouring solution. &nbsp;[<a href=3D"https://dl.acm.org/d=
