2"><h3>5.2 Results</h3><div role=3D"paragraph">This subsection summarises t=
he experimental results of four methods. We presented three group datasets =
(c01-07 avg, c08-14 avg and c15-c21 avg). First, the performance of the sta=
ndalone GA is evaluated under nine parameter settings. Second, the SA metho=
d is tested under four parameter settings Third, a hybrid GA+SA approach is=
 implemented to combine the strengths of both algorithms. Finally, the scal=
ability analysis (2-5 times the original data) examines how the method perf=
orms as the dataset size increases.</div><section id=3D"sec-5-2-1"><h4>5.2.=
1 Genetic Algorithm Performance.</h4><div role=3D"paragraph">For the standa=
lone GA, multiple combinations of core parameters were tested, including po=
pulation size: 30, 100 and 150, mutation rate: 0.1, 0.2 and 0.3, and genera=
tion count: 50, 100 and 200 &nbsp;[<a href=3D"https://dl.acm.org/doi/full/1=
