</section><section id=3D"sec-6"><h2>6 Conclusion</h2><div role=3D"paragraph=
">This paper presented a hybrid approach for the UCTTP problem, integrating=
 the global search ability of GA with the local refinement of SA. The resul=
t was evaluated on the ITC-2007 stack3 benchmark and its extended dataset. =
Experimental results demonstrated that GA more efficiently than SA generate=
s feasible timetables with zero hard-constraint violations under small to m=
edium datasets but has caused a fall into local optimum under large dataset=
s, while the hybrid GA+SA model further improves. By adopting a stop termin=
ation strategy once hard constraints are satisfied, our implementation cost=
 an efficient runtime.</div><div role=3D"paragraph">However, this efficienc=
y has not included optimising soft-constraint penalties, which are also ess=
ential for generating high-quality timetables in real-world applications. I=
n future work, this framework will be extended to soft-constraint optimisat=
ion, allowing us to directly compare penalty-based solution quality.</div><=
